## 5. Skill Execution Protocol & Self-Correction Engine

The workflow within `SKILL.md` operates as an autonomous self-healing loop:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Agent as Antigravity Agent
    participant Indexer as repo_indexer.py
    participant File as GEMINI.md
    participant Validator as validate_gemini_md.py

    User->>Agent: "Initialize/Update GEMINI.md"
    Agent->>Indexer: Run --root . --json
    Indexer-->>Agent: Ground-truth JSON metadata
    Agent->>File: Write candidate GEMINI.md (5-tier anatomy)
    
    loop Self-Correction (Max 2 Attempts)
        Agent->>Validator: Run validate_gemini_md.py --json
        Validator-->>Agent: Exit Code & Diagnostic JSON
        alt Exit Code == 0
            Agent-->>User: Success (Report token & line metrics)
        else Exit Code != 0 and Retry < 2
            Agent->>Agent: Parse error code (e.g., ERR_BUDGET_EXCEEDED, ERR_BROKEN_LINK)
            Agent->>File: Apply targeted corrective edits
        else Exit Code != 0 and Retry >= 2
            Agent-->>User: Halt with structured diagnostic failure report
        end
    end
```

### 5.1 Remediation Strategies by Error Code

* **`ERR_BUDGET_EXCEEDED` $\rightarrow$ Targeted Subtraction Protocol**:
  1. Trigger the "Inferable Rule": Scan Section 3 and strip all linter-enforced formatting and language boilerplate.
  2. Convert verbose narrative paragraphs in Section 2 into concise ASCII component diagrams or markdown mapping tables.
  3. Re-calculate metrics.
* **`ERR_BROKEN_LINK` $\rightarrow$ Path Resolution Protocol**:
  1. Read the invalid path from the validator's JSON diagnostic payload.
  2. Search the indexer's cached file tree for the closest matching basename.
  3. Rewrite the markdown link to the corrected relative path or remove it if obsolete.
* **`ERR_SCHEMA_INVALID` $\rightarrow$ Frontmatter Normalization**:
  1. Identify missing or malformed keys.
  2. Re-inject the required frontmatter skeleton from `assets/gemini_template.md`.

